1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,105
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,105 --> 00:00:09,005
This morning the system named no pick, so tonight there is nothing to grade.

3
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:13,740
No setup, no trade, no loss — that is the discipline working.

4
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:18,676
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

5
00:00:18,676 --> 00:00:24,085
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:27,569
On the day, the book is up 498 dollars.

7
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:30,817
Broadcom (AVGO) leads, +6.6 percent.

8
00:00:30,817 --> 00:00:33,975
APA Corporation (APA) lags at -2.9.

9
00:00:33,975 --> 00:00:39,750
The checklist carries 1 item; details are in the written report.

10
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:43,276
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

11
00:00:43,232 --> 00:00:50,558
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

12
00:00:50,558 --> 00:01:01,080
12 positions, led by State Street SPDR S&P Oil & Gas Exploration & Production ETF, ticker XOP, Target, ticker TGT, Airbnb, ticker ABNB.

13
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:11,679
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

14
00:01:11,653 --> 00:01:16,590
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

15
00:01:16,590 --> 00:01:19,059
Every morning OROS proposes.

16
00:01:19,059 --> 00:01:29,903
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

17
00:01:29,903 --> 00:01:33,958
Inside the book today: 7 positions up, 5 down.

18
00:01:33,958 --> 00:01:36,427
Best, AVGO at +6.61 percent.

19
00:01:36,427 --> 00:01:38,190
Worst, APA at -2.90.

20
00:01:38,190 --> 00:01:43,304
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

21
00:01:43,304 --> 00:01:50,621
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -8.50% per trade over 167 graded positions.

22
00:01:50,621 --> 00:01:57,851
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 25% position size.

23
00:01:57,851 --> 00:02:03,140
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

24
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:19,362
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 245 names close the day in Stage 2; 3 new invalidations queue exit reviews; position size stays cut to 25% until the record earns it back.

25
00:02:19,316 --> 00:02:21,574
Over to the sports desk.

26
00:02:21,574 --> 00:02:31,455
Day 18 of 18 in the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

27
00:02:31,455 --> 00:02:37,759
In first place, the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, at 104,161.

28
00:02:37,759 --> 00:02:43,311
Then the index fund, in gray, 1.5 thousand back at 102,669.

29
00:02:43,311 --> 00:02:50,651
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 4.1 thousand back at 100,091.

30
00:02:50,651 --> 00:02:52,250
That's the final.

31
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:55,356
The full season review is coming.

32
00:02:55,356 --> 00:03:00,249
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

33
00:03:00,249 --> 00:03:02,131
Nothing is restated.

34
00:03:02,131 --> 00:03:11,038
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

35
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:18,335
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

36
00:03:18,335 --> 00:03:20,576
Nothing here is financial advice.

37
00:03:20,576 --> 00:03:23,565
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
